    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "True or False? Let $A$ and $B$ be sets in a universal set $U$.\n\n$\\overline{A\\cup B}=\\overline A\\cap\\overline B$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "True.",
      "worked": "True. Being outside $A\\cup B$ means being outside both $A$ and $B$. These are exactly the elements common to $\\overline A$ and $\\overline B$.",
